About Nebius:

Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.

Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.

Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;D.

About the role

Location: Israel - Modiin (Training) / Masmia (Work Location) &nbsp;
Duration: 6 months &nbsp;
Start date: December 2026 &nbsp;
Compensation: Paid &nbsp;
Eligibility: Recent Graduate or Early Career specialist&nbsp;
Work authorization: Permitted to work in the job's location

Role Description &nbsp;

As an&nbsp; Data Center Technician (Early Talent) , you will gain hands-on experience maintaining and supporting IT infrastructure within our data centers, including modern GPU cloud cluster technologies. &nbsp;

You will learn to troubleshoot and resolve hardware issues, perform physical hardware repairs, support infrastructure maintenance, and ensure the smooth operation of critical systems. &nbsp;

This is a 6-month, hands-on technical training program designed for individuals looking to build a long-term career in data center operations and IT infrastructure. &nbsp;

Program Structure &amp; Working Conditions &nbsp;

The program consists of two phases: &nbsp;

• Month 1 - Training: Full-time training in Modiin, Monday to Friday, 9:00-17:00. &nbsp;

• Months 2 - 6 - On-site Operations: Shift-based work at our Masmia data center, following a&nbsp; 4-days-on / 4-days-off rotation , including night shifts and weekends. &nbsp;

Important requirements: &nbsp;

• A valid driver’s license and access to your own car are required, as public transportation to the Masmia site is unavailable during night shifts. &nbsp;

• The role involves physical work, including prolonged standing, working with hardware equipment, and using ladders. &nbsp;

• You must be comfortable working rotating shifts, including nights and weekends. &nbsp;

• You must be able to read and understand technical documentation in English. &nbsp;

Successful participants may be considered for a full-time L1 IT Technician position upon completing the program, subject to performance and available headcount. &nbsp;

Skills You Will Learn &nbsp;

• Diagnosing and resolving IT hardware issues while ensuring continuous support of the data center’s IT infrastructure. &nbsp;

• Collaborating effectively with internal teams and external contractors to address technical and operational challenges. &nbsp;

• Installing, upgrading, replacing, and dismantling hardware based on operational requirements. &nbsp;

• Managing and maintaining fiber optic cables, patch cords, and network connectivity. &nbsp;

• Planning, executing, and monitoring routine IT maintenance tasks to support infrastructure reliability. &nbsp;

• Processing Return Merchandise Authorizations (RMAs) in accordance with established procedures. &nbsp;

• Creating and maintaining technical documentation for hardware configuration, troubleshooting, and maintenance. &nbsp;

• Working cross-functionally with infrastructure, networking, and other technical teams. &nbsp;

We Expect You to Have &nbsp;

• Education or training in a relevant technical field, such as IT, computer hardware, electronics, networking, or practical engineering, through a technical college, Handesaim program, vocational training, or military technical training. &nbsp;

• A strong interest in pursuing a hands-on technical career in data center operations and IT infrastructure. &nbsp;

